config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	bool "Domoticz 2026.4"
	depends on FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_1_0_58_MIN
	depends on FREETZ_TARGET_IPV6_SUPPORT
	select FREETZ_LIB_STDCXXLIB
	select FREETZ_LIB_libboost_thread
	select FREETZ_LIB_libz
	select FREETZ_LIB_libcurl
	select FREETZ_LIB_libcrypto
	select FREETZ_LIB_libssl
	select FREETZ_LIB_libsqlite3
	select FREETZ_LIB_liblua
	select FREETZ_LIB_libusb0
	select FREETZ_LIB_libusb1
	select FREETZ_LIB_libatomic
	select FREETZ_LIB_libopenzwave
	select FREETZ_LIB_libtelldus_core
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3
	select FREETZ_LIB_libpython3
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_MOSQUITTO
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_MOSQUITTO_CLIENTS
	default n
	help
		Domoticz is a lightweight home automation system: it lets you monitor
		and control lights, switches, sensors, thermostats, media players and
		many other devices from a web browser.

		Build characteristics in Freetz:

		 - Boost (Boost.Asio, Boost.Signals2, Boost.Thread) is provided by the
		   boost package, which is cross-built with b2 and also installs the
		   BoostConfig.cmake that CMake 4 requires (FindBoost was removed).
		 - SQLite, OpenSSL, zlib, libcurl, libusb, Lua 5.4 and libmosquitto
		   (the MQTT client library).
		 - The four git submodules of the 2026.4 tag (extern/jsoncpp,
		   extern/minizip, extern/jwtcpp, extern/libwebem) are downloaded and
		   unpacked by the package, because GitHub source archives never
		   contain submodule contents.
		 - Embedded Python plugin support is enabled (links libpython3.14),
		   dzVents/Lua event scripts use the tree's Lua 5.4.
		 - The built-in updater is disabled. OpenZWave (Z-Wave) and Telldus
		   (Tellstick) are compiled in: the OpenZWave device database is
		   installed in /usr/share/domoticz/Config, from which Domoticz loads
		   it at run time. Telldus only provides the client library here, so
		   a Tellstick additionally needs the telldusd daemon.

		Web interface: http://fritz.box:8080/ (configurable in
		/mod/etc/default.domoticz/domoticz.cfg)
